        confer "The appellant also billed for a power wheelchair base (K0870) and lead acid battery (E2363) furnished on the same date of service".
    the HCPCS code of the power wheelchair is "K0870",
        confer "The appellant also billed for a power wheelchair base (K0870) and lead acid battery (E2363) furnished on the same date of service".
    the power wheelchair is furnished to the beneficiary,
        confer "The beneficiary purchased a power wheelchair with certain accessories on January 6, 2010".
    the date of service of claim 5 is 2010-01-06,
        confer "The beneficiary purchased a power wheelchair with certain accessories on January 6, 2010".
    the medical record of the beneficiary documents inclusion body myositis,
        confer "The beneficiary is diagnosed with inclusion body myositis".
    the order for the power wheelchair is signed by the treating practitioner,
        confer "pursuant to a prescription and certificate of medical necessity issued by his physician".
    the order for the seat elevation system is signed by the treating practitioner,
        confer "pursuant to a prescription and certificate of medical necessity issued by his physician".
    rn expects answers [].
    pay expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].
    dme expects answers [].

% M-10-1590, S.C.S. (20 January 2011). A power standing system (E2301)
% furnished 26 July 2007 by Wheelchair Works as an accessory of the existing
% power wheelchair of a man with spinal muscular atrophy type II, unable to
% walk or stand; his physicians' letters and an independent medical expert
% retained by the ALJ support its medical benefit; the contractor's medical
% director testified that its primary uses are reaching high surfaces and
% eye-level social interaction.
% Council: not covered — Policy Article A19846 ("a power standing feature
% (E2301) is noncovered because it is not primarily medical in nature") is
% owed substantial deference, the literature showing no consensus that a
% standing system prevents the complications of sitting; the system is not
% DME, so section 1879 does not apply and the beneficiary is liable.
% Model: not reasonable and necessary — agrees: E2301 is within the
% wheelchair options policy's scope and no rule covers it (the current
% Article A52504 keeps the exclusion), so the query fails at question. The
% base is not claimed (its code is not stated), and the physicians' opinion
% of medical benefit has no finding to go to. Candidate templates: "*an
% item* is of medical benefit to *a beneficiary*", "*an item* is primarily
% and customarily used for a nonmedical purpose" (the negation of the
% dmepos.le characteristic).
scenario scs_partb is, as stated in Council decision scs partb:
    claim 1 is for the standing system,
        confer "a power standing system (HCPCS E2301) wheelchair accessory furnished to the beneficiary by Wheelchair Works, Inc. (supplier) on July 26, 2007".
    the HCPCS code of the standing system is "E2301",
        confer "a power standing system (HCPCS E2301) wheelchair accessory".
    the standing system is furnished to SCS,
        confer "a power standing system (PSS) furnished to him by the supplier on July 26, 2007, as an accessory to an existing power wheelchair".
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2007-07-26,
        confer "furnished to him by the supplier on July 26, 2007".
    the standing system is an accessory of the power wheelchair,
        confer "as an accessory to an existing power wheelchair".
    the medical record of SCS documents spinal muscular atrophy,
        confer "The beneficiary is diagnosed with Spinal Muscle Atrophy (SMA, Type II)".
    the residence of SCS is private residence,
        confer "to allow access to higher surfaces in the home (such as countertops)".
    rn expects answers [].
    pay expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].
    dme expects answers [].

% M-12-1359, ATG Connecticut d/b/a ATG Rehab (12 December 2012). A power
% articulating foot platform (Tru-Balance 2, coded K0108 by the PDAC:
% "wheelchair component or accessory, not otherwise specified") furnished 28
% May 2010 as part of the power wheelchair of a 47-year-old man with ALS,
% after a face-to-face examination, a physical therapist's functional
% mobility evaluation, a home accessibility evaluation and an affirmative
% ADMC covering the platform; Medicare paid it at the fee of the power leg
% elevation system E1010 ($828.10) and the supplier sought a percentage of
% the retail price.
% Council: adopts the ALJ — coverage was never in dispute (the ADMC
% established medical necessity but "does not extend to the price"); K0108
% is carrier priced by gap-filling, and the contractor may treat the
% platform as comparable to E1010 (a dedicated motor raising the legs
% independently of tilt and recline).
% Model: outside its scope — K0108 belongs to no modelled policy (the query
% fails at applicability), and the model has no pricing: the dispute is not
% one it decides. The base's code is not stated and the base is not
% claimed; the ADMC's date is not given, so the prior-authorization fact of
% dmepos.le cannot be dated; the face-to-face examination has no date and
% the therapist's evaluation does not say she had no financial relationship
% with the supplier. Had the platform been billed as E1010, the power
% seating rule of wheelchair_options.le would need a covered base, the
% specialty evaluation and the ATP, and the finding "power seating system
% needed" — the decision reports the evaluations but none of their
% findings. Candidate templates: "*a code* is priced by comparison with *an
% other code*", "the fee schedule amount of *a code* is *an amount*", "an
% advance determination of Medicare coverage for *an item* was affirmed"
% (undated).
scenario m-12-1359 is, as stated in Council decision m 12 1359:
    claim 1 is for the foot platform,
        confer "a power articulating foot platform furnished to the beneficiary as part of a power wheelchair".
    the HCPCS code of the foot platform is "K0108",
        confer "namely HCPCS code K0108".
    the foot platform is furnished to the beneficiary,
        confer "a power articulating foot platform furnished to the beneficiary as part of a power wheelchair".
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2010-05-28,
        confer "The appellant supplied the wheelchair and accessories on May 28, 2010".
    the foot platform is an accessory of the power wheelchair,
        confer "furnished to the beneficiary as part of a power wheelchair".
    the medical record of the beneficiary documents amyotrophic lateral sclerosis,
        confer "had been diagnosed with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS)".
    the supplier performed an on-site evaluation of the home for the power wheelchair,
        confer "a home accessibility evaluation".
    rn expects answers [].
    pay expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].
